2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] This is a correct extraction of key ELF header fields. Here's a quick breakdown of what each field
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] represents:
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] 1. e_entry (0x18/24): The program entry point address (where execution starts)
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] 2. e_phoff (0x1C/28): Offset to program header table in the file
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] 3. e_shoff (0x20/32): Offset to section header table (useful for symbols/debug info)
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] 4. e_phentsize (0x2A/42): Size of each program header entry (typically 32 bytes for 32-bit
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] ELF)
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] 5. e_phnum (0x2C/44): Number of program header entries
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] For a more complete ELF loader, you might also want:
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] const e_shentsize = view.getUint16(46, true); // Section header entry size
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] const e_shnum = view.getUint16(48, true);    // Number of section headers
2025-08-05 13:31:07 [deepseek-chat] const e_shstrndx = view.getUint16(50, true); // Section name string table index
