2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] 1) Goals (what persona layer gives you)
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Consistent assistant behavior per model/account/session (tone, brevity, safety rules).
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Easy A/B testing of different persona prompts.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Faster iteration and fewer “blunders” by making expectations explicit.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Auditability (which persona generated which answer).
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] 2) Persona types (pick as needed)
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Model persona: attached to a specific model/version (e.g., “concise-researcher” for Llama,
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] “cautious-auditor” for Claude).
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Session persona: applied for a particular chat or user session (temporary, overrides defaults).
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - User persona: per user preferences (verbosity, style).
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Experiment persona: ephemeral variants for A/B tests.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] 3) Where to store them (Slop Fountain integration)
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Add a persona registry in the existing forge state (roha.personas) and a persona field on
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] roha.mut entries:
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini]   - roha.personas = { id: { name, system, guide, tags, created, version } }
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini]   - roha.mut[model].persona = personaId (default persona for that model)
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Allow session override: rohaHistory or roha.session to temporarily bind a persona.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Record persona id and version in message metadata/logs so results are traceable.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] 4) Prompt composition (recommended layered approach)
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - system base: firm safety & meta rules (never include secrets, privacy rules).
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - persona system: tone + instructions (one-liners, subtle constraints).
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - rohaGuide: shared operational hints (current short rules you’re iterating on).
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - per-request: user message and any few-shot examples.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Compose as: [system base] + [persona system] + [rohaGuide/system prompt] + [history/few-shot] →
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] payload.messages[0..]
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] 5) Persona content guidelines (short, subtle, professional)
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] Make each persona short (1–3 lines), explicit about assumptions, and include a “self-check” step.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] Examples (single-line to paste into persona.system):
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - "Note assumptions briefly. Sanity-check examples. Prefer cautious, minimal answers."
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - "State confidence (low/med/high) for nontrivial claims and ask one focused clarifying question if
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] needed."
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - "Professional researcher: concise, cite facts when possible, flag uncertainties."
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] 6) Safety & prompt-injection defenses
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Never persist secrets inside persona text. Keep only operational rules and style.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Strip user-provided system messages or disallow user->system replacements unless explicitly
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] permitted.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Add a short validator: if incoming message contains "system:" or function-calling payload
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] overrides, warn and ignore user-supplied system content unless session is privileged.
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] 7) A/B testing & metrics
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Tag each request with variant id (personaId or experimentId).
2025-08-08 10:46:41 [gpt-5-mini] - Randomize assignments for users/requests.
