2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] Fountain.
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] Storage location (recommendation)
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] - Keep personas separate from mutable state: add a new read‑only file personas.json next to
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] modelspecs.json rather than mutating modelspecs.json. This makes intent clear and simplifies
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] ACLs/auditing.
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] - Store personas in the repo (tracked by git) and load at startup. Treat the file as authoritative
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] and immutable at runtime.
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] Persona data model (what each persona contains)
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] - id (string, stable key)
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] - name (human label)
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] - system (1–3 short lines: persona system prompt)
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] - guide (optional short operational hints)
2025-08-08 10:49:08 [gpt-5-mini] - tags (array: safety/experiment/role)
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - version (semver or integer)
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - createdby, createdat, changelog (metadata)
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - immutable: true (explicit marker that runtime must not write)
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] Read‑only enforcement
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - File-level: mark personas.json read-only (filesystem perms) and keep it under source control.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Runtime: on startup compute checksum (SHA256) and refuse any operation that writes personas.json
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] or any persona entry. Expose a clear error if a write is attempted.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Admin edits: require out‑of‑band changes (git commit / PR) and then restart, or provide a
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] privileged CLI that accepts a signed update (if you want hot updates).
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] How to apply personas at runtime
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Load personas.json at startup and validate against schema.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - roha.mut[model].persona = personaId (set from modelspecs.json or a default mapping at startup).
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] Persist mapping in roha (mutable) if you want per‑model default.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Compose messages as: [base system] + [personas[personaId].system] + [rohaGuide/system hints] +
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] [history].
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Session overrides: allow ephemeral session persona (in-memory only, not saved to personas.json or
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] roha file) — useful for experiments.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] Logging & audit
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Tag every request with personaId and persona.version in rohaHistory/logs.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Record persona checksum (or file version) in forge metadata so you can reproduce exact persona
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] text used for any reply.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Keep change history in git and include changelog in persona metadata.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] Safety / policy
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Persona text must not include secrets or provider API keys.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Validate persona system content to avoid conflicting system instructions (e.g., no "allow user to
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] change system prompt" lines).
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Optionally add a small linter that flags personas that are too long, contain "do anything"
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] language, or try to exfiltrate data.
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] Versioning & experiments
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Use persona.version to A/B test variants (A and B are separate persona ids/versions).
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - Randomize assignment and log variant id per request (as earlier discussed).
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] Migration and compatibility
2025-08-08 10:49:09 [gpt-5-mini] - If you currently store persona-like text in modelspecs, migrate those entries into personas.json
