2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] I've compiled Rongorongo information for the biblispec project! This is a fascinating addition -
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] one of the most mysterious writing systems in the world.
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] • Key highlights of Rongorongo:*
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] - Unique boustrophedon style - alternating line directions (reverse boustrophedon)
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] - ~25 surviving artifacts - mostly wooden tablets called "kohau"
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] - Undeciphered status - despite 150+ years of attempts
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] - Rapa Nui origin - Easter Island's indigenous script
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] - Glyphic nature - mixture of anthropomorphic, zoomorphic, and geometric forms
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] The Unicode coverage is limited (just 4 basic characters), but the cultural and linguistic
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] significance is enormous. This represents one of the few independent writing system inventions in
2025-08-08 19:54:14 [claude-sonnet-4] Polynesia.
