2025-08-09 10:56:32 [nitro@ryzen5] to create nitro_repos_stats.csv can the bat file parse the nitro_repos.csv and measure size and privacy of each dir ?
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] Yes, the batch file can be enhanced to parse the CSV and gather stats. Here's a modified version
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] that creates `nitroreposstats.csv`:
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] @echo off
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] setlocal EnableDelayedExpansion
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] echo Analyzing repository statistics...
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] REM Create header for stats file
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] echo owner,repo,exists,size_kb,private > nitro_repos_stats.csv
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] for /f "tokens=1,2 delims=," %%a in (nitro_repos.csv) do (
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]     call :analyze_repo %%a %%b
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] )
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] echo Repository analysis complete.
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] pause
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] goto :eof
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] :analyze_repo
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] set "owner=%1"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] set "repo=%2"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] set "repo_path=nitrologic\%repo%"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] set "exists=false"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] set "size_kb=0"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] set "private=unknown"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] echo Analyzing %owner%/%repo%...
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] REM Check if directory exists
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] if exist "%repo_path%" (
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]     set "exists=true"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]     REM Calculate directory size using PowerShell
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]     for /f %%i in ('powershell -command "(Get-ChildItem -Path '%repo_path%' -Recurse -File | Measure-Object -Property Length -Sum).Sum / 1KB"') do (
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]         set "size_kb=%%i"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]     )
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]     REM Check if it's a private repo by looking for .git/config
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]     if exist "%repo_path%\.git\config" (
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]         findstr /c:"github.com/%owner%/%repo%" "%repo_path%\.git\config" >nul 2>&1
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]         if !ERRORLEVEL! equ 0 (
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]             REM Could check GitHub API here, but for now mark as public
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]             set "private=false"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]         )
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4]     )
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] )
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] REM Round size to integer
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] for /f %%j in ('powershell -command "[math]::Round(%size_kb%)"') do set "size_kb=%%j"
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] echo %owner%,%repo%,!exists!,!size_kb!,!private! >> nitro_repos_stats.csv
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] goto :eof
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] This enhanced version will:
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] - Check if each repo directory exists locally
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] - Calculate directory size in KB using PowerShell
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] - Attempt to determine privacy status (though full GitHub API integration would be needed for
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] accurate private/public detection)
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] - Output results to `nitroreposstats.csv` with columns: owner, repo, exists, size_kb,
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] private
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] The size calculation uses PowerShell for accuracy, and the privacy detection is basic but could be
2025-08-09 10:56:45 [claude-sonnet-4] enhanced with GitHub API calls if needed.
