2025-08-09 11:07:09 [nitro@ryzen5] is there a git command that can fill in a few basic stats
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] Yes! Git has several commands that can provide repository statistics. Here are some useful ones for
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] your analysis:
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] • Basic Git Stats Commands:*
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4]  Get total commit count
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] git rev-list --count HEAD
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4]  Get number of contributors
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] git shortlog -sn | wc -l
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4]  Get repository size (local .git folder)
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] git count-objects -vH
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4]  Get last commit date
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] git log -1 --format=%cd --date=short
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4]  Get branch count
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] git branch -a | wc -l
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4]  Get file count (tracked files)
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] git ls-files | wc -l
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4]  Get language stats (if you have git-linguist)
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] git-linguist --breakdown
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] • For your clonestat.bat, you could add:*
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] :analyse
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 	set "owner=%1"
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 	set "repo=%2"
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 	set "path=nitrologic\%repo%"
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 	if exist "%path%" (
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 		cd /d "%path%"
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 		rem Get commit count
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 		for /f %%i in ('git rev-list --count HEAD 2^>nul') do set "commits=%%i"
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 		if "%commits%"=="" set "commits=0"
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 		rem Get last commit date
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 		for /f %%i in ('git log -1 --format^=%%cd --date^=short 2^>nul') do set "lastcommit=%%i"
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 		if "%lastcommit%"=="" set "lastcommit=none"
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 		rem Get file count
2025-08-09 11:07:19 [claude-sonnet-4] 		for /f %%i in ('git ls-files ^| find /c /v ""') do set "files=%%i"
