2025-08-10 11:34:10 [deepseek-chat] Glagolitic Unicode Block (U+2C00–U+2C5F)
2025-08-10 11:34:10 [deepseek-chat] Overview
2025-08-10 11:34:10 [deepseek-chat] - Origin: Created by Saints Cyril and Methodius in the 9th century for Slavic liturgical
2025-08-10 11:34:10 [deepseek-chat] texts (predates Cyrillic!).
2025-08-10 11:34:10 [deepseek-chat] - Usage: Early Slavic manuscripts, Croatian Church Slavonic (rarely used today).
2025-08-10 11:34:10 [deepseek-chat] - Design: Curvy, almost runic-like letters with symbolic names (e.g., Ⰱ "Buki" = "beech
2025-08-10 11:34:10 [deepseek-chat] tree").
2025-08-10 11:34:10 [deepseek-chat] - Unicode Support: Stable (since Unicode 4.1, 2005). Fonts like Noto Sans
2025-08-10 11:34:10 [deepseek-chat] Glagolitic or Segoe UI Historic display it correctly.
