2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] Yes — you can derive a reliable filename from several pieces of metadata (some local, some from the
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] TTS response). Quick summary and recommendations:
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] Possible metadata to use
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - Local/derived:
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - timestamp (UTC or unix hex) — always available and unique.
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - provider/account or model (e.g., "openai", "gpt-4o-mini-tts" or your grokModel) — from your
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] config/payload.
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - voice and format parameters you requested (voice, format).
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - rohaNic / username or session id.
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - short content snippet (sanitised) or short hash of the input text (SHA-1/SHA-256 truncated) —
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] avoid long filenames or unsafe chars.
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - Response headers (inspect before writing):
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - Content-Type (e.g., audio/mpeg) → use to decide extension.
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - Content-Disposition (some APIs include filename).
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - Any provider-specific metadata returned in JSON or headers.
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] Filename patterns (pick one)
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - timestampprovidermodelvoicehash.ext
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - Example: 20250810T153000openaigpt4o-minialloy3f2a8c.mp3
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - timestampusersnippet.ext
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - Example: 20250810jonhello-world.mp3 (shorten/snippet and sanitize)
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - timestamp_hash.json + audio file
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini]   - Example: 64b3a7.json (metadata sidecar) + 64b3a7.mp3 (keeps filenames short)
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] Extension mapping from Content-Type
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - audio/mpeg → .mp3
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - audio/ogg; codecs=opus or audio/opus → .opus or .ogg
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - audio/wav or audio/x-wav → .wav
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - audio/flac → .flac
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - audio/aac or audio/mp4 → .aac or .mp4
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] (Fall back to requested format or .bin)
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] Other practical tips
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - Sanitize filenames (strip/replace non-alphanumeric, limit length).
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - Prefer a short hash of text (e.g., first 8–12 hex chars of SHA-256) rather than the full text.
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] - Save a JSON sidecar or add an entry to roha.forge with metadata (path, model, voice, format,
2025-08-11 10:22:32 [gpt-5-mini] timestamp, original text hash) so you can track provenance.
