2025-08-11 11:12:30 [gpt-5-mini] - If flush returns a Promise/thenable, await waits for resolution/rejection. If it returns a
2025-08-11 11:12:30 [gpt-5-mini] non-promise value, await immediately yields that value.
2025-08-11 11:12:30 [gpt-5-mini] - In tests people commonly use helpers named flush/flushPromises to wait for pending microtasks or
2025-08-11 11:12:30 [gpt-5-mini] use setTimeout(…,0) to wait a macrotask. Frameworks also provide their own helpers
