2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] The number 47 in BCP47 refers to Best Current Practice 47, an IETF
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] (Internet Engineering Task Force) document that standardizes language tags for identifying
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] languages, scripts, regions, and variants.
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] Why "BCP47"?
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] - BCP stands for Best Current Practice, a series of IETF documents that provide
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] guidelines or standards.
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] - 47 is simply the document number assigned to this specific standard.
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] What It Does:
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] BCP47 defines the structure for language tags (like `en-US`, `fr-FR`, `ja-JP`), ensuring
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] consistency in software, localization, and internationalization. It combines:
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] 1. ISO 639 (language codes, e.g., `en` for English).
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] 2. ISO 3166 (region codes, e.g., `US` for the United States).
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] 3. Optional subtags for scripts, variants, etc.
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] Your JSON snippet lists common BCP47-compliant language tags, each pairing a language with its
2025-08-11 13:19:35 [deepseek-chat] region (e.g., `de-DE` for German in Germany).
