2025-08-11 13:21:31 [deepseek-chat] mapping) would be more efficient and semantically clearer than an array.
2025-08-11 13:21:31 [deepseek-chat] Why an Object Makes More Sense:
2025-08-11 13:21:31 [deepseek-chat] 1. Faster Lookups: Checking if a tag exists (e.g., `"fr-FR"`) is `O(1)` with an object vs.
2025-08-11 13:21:31 [deepseek-chat] `O(n)` with an array.
2025-08-11 13:21:31 [deepseek-chat] 2. Avoids Redundancy: No need to repeat `language`/`code` pairs—the key is the
2025-08-11 13:21:31 [deepseek-chat] BCP47 tag.
2025-08-11 13:21:31 [deepseek-chat] 3. Clearer Intent: Objects imply unordered, unique keys, while arrays imply ordered
2025-08-11 13:21:31 [deepseek-chat] sequences.
