2025-08-11 15:17:01 [deepseek-chat] modern features, and a streamlined development experience.
2025-08-11 15:17:01 [deepseek-chat] In your code snippet, `Buffer.from(audioData, "base64")` is used to decode a base64-encoded string
2025-08-11 15:17:01 [deepseek-chat] (`audioData`) into a binary buffer (`audioBuffer`).
2025-08-11 15:17:01 [deepseek-chat] If you're using Deno, you might need to adjust the code slightly because Deno doesn't natively
2025-08-11 15:17:01 [deepseek-chat] include the `Buffer` class like Node.js. Instead, you can use the `TextEncoder`/`TextDecoder` APIs
2025-08-11 15:17:01 [deepseek-chat] or the `atob` function for base64 decoding in Deno.
