2025-08-11 15:20:04 [nitro@ryzen5] geminiSay is logging correct mime64 but i was hoping to use mp3?
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] Gemini does not natively support MP3 encoding. While you can log or handle base64-encoded audio
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] data (e.g., `mimeType: "audio/mpeg"`), encoding raw audio to MP3 would require an external library
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] or tool. Here are your options:
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] 1. Client-Side Encoding:
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat]    Use a JavaScript library like [lamejs](https://github.com/zhuker/lamejs) to encode audio to MP3
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] in the browser before sending it to Gemini.
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] 2. Server-Side Encoding:
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat]    Process the audio on a backend service (e.g., Node.js with [`ffmpeg`](https://ffmpeg.org/) or
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] Python with [`pydub`](https://github.com/jiaaro/pydub)).
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] 3. Workaround:
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat]    If you only need playback (not encoding), ensure the audio data is already in MP3 format before
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] passing it to Gemini.
2025-08-11 15:20:19 [deepseek-chat] Let me know if you'd like code examples for any of these approaches!
