2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] You're right — two things went wrong in that run:
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] 1) Git branch-tracking mismatch
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - Error "Your configuration specifies to merge with the ref 'refs/heads/master' ... but no such ref
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] was fetched" means the local branch is configured to merge with origin/master, but the remote
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] doesn't have master (it uses main or another name). Fix by fetching and repointing the local branch
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] to the remote default (or renaming the local branch).
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] Suggested repair steps inside the nitrocircuit repo:
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - cd to the repo (or popd back until you reach it).
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - git fetch origin
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - git remote show origin   (see which branch is HEAD — usually "main")
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - If your local branch is master but remote is main:
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini]   - git branch -m master main
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini]   - git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/main main
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini]   - git pull --ff-only
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - Or if the local branch exists as main already but tracking is wrong:
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini]   - git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/main main
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini]   - git pull --ff-only
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] 2) The refresh script left you in the wrong directory
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - Your refresh used "pushd ... && git pull && popd". Because the git pull failed, the && prevented
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] popd from running, leaving you inside nitrologic\nitrocircuit. Subsequent pushd calls then
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] attempted paths relative to that nested CWD and failed ("The system cannot find the path
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] specified").
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] How to avoid this next time
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - Ensure popd runs even if git pull fails (don’t make popd conditional on pull success). In batch
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] files use a sequence that always executes popd after pushd, or wrap pull in a conditional that
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] still falls through to popd.
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - Add a git-fetch-first step and set origin HEAD if you want pulls to follow the remote default
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] (git fetch origin; git remote set-head origin -a).
2025-08-12 09:25:04 [gpt-5-mini] - Log failures and continue so a single repo error doesn’t break the directory stack.
