2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] What to check and why
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - git status --porcelain => local uncommitted changes & untracked files.
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - git fetch + compare local vs remote upstream => whether remote has new commits to pull.
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - git diff origin/<branch>..HEAD or HEAD..origin/<branch> => what changed between local and remote.
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - git ls-files -o --exclude-standard => files on disk that are git‑ignored or untracked.
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] Windows (cmd) quick loop (safe: uses git -C so cwd never changes)
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] for /d %%D in ("nitrologic\*") do (
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	echo === %%~nxD ===
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	if exist "%%D\.git" (
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		"C:\Program Files\Git\bin\git.exe" -C "%%D" fetch --quiet
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		"C:\Program Files\Git\bin\git.exe" -C "%%D" status --porcelain
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		"C:\Program Files\Git\bin\git.exe" -C "%%D" rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name @{u}
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 2>nul ||
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 			(echo No upstream configured)
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	) else (
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		echo Skipping (no .git)
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	)
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] )
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] PowerShell (more readable; shows upstream vs local)
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] Get-ChildItem -Directory nitrologic | ForEach-Object {
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	Write-Host "=== $($_.Name) ==="
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	if (Test-Path (Join-Path $_.FullName ".git")) {
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		git -C $_.FullName fetch --quiet
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		git -C $_.FullName status --porcelain
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		try {
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 			$up = git -C $_.FullName rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name @{u}
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 			git -C $_.FullName rev-list --left-right --count $up...HEAD
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		} catch {
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 			Write-Host "No upstream configured"
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		}
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	} else { Write-Host "Skipping (no .git)" }
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] }
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] Bash (POSIX / Git Bash / WSL)
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] for d in nitrologic/*/; do
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	[ -d "$d/.git" ] || continue
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	echo "=== ${d%/} ==="
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	git -C "$d" fetch --quiet
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	git -C "$d" status --porcelain
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	upstream=$(git -C "$d" rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name @{u} 2>/dev/null || true)
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	if [ -n "$upstream" ]; then
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		git -C "$d" rev-list --left-right --count "$upstream...HEAD"
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	else
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 		echo "No upstream configured"
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] 	fi
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] done
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] Interpreting results
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - status lines (porcelain) — anything listed is uncommitted/untracked; empty = clean.
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - rev-list output "X Y" means: X commits the upstream is ahead of you (you should pull), Y commits
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] you are ahead of upstream (local commits not pushed).
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - "No upstream configured" means the local branch has no tracking branch (this caused your earlier
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] master/main error).
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - To see actual file diffs: git -C repo diff --name-status origin/main..HEAD (or the upstream
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] branch).
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] Detect files on disk that are not in git (untracked/ignored)
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - git -C repo ls-files -o --exclude-standard  => untracked (not ignored)
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - git -C repo ls-files --others --exclude-standard  => same
2025-08-12 09:38:02 [gpt-5-mini] - git -C repo ls-files -i --exclude-standard => ignored files
