2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat] To silently fetch and display the remote URL of a Git repository in a batch file (without
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat] showing the `git` command itself due to `@echo off`), you can use one of these methods:
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat] Method 1: Redirect Output to a File
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat] @echo off
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat] for /D %%D in ("nitrologic\*") do (
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat]     if exist "%%D\.git" (
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat]         git -C "%%D" remote -v > remote_url.txt
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat]         type remote_url.txt
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat]         del remote_url.txt
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat]     )
2025-08-12 10:06:28 [deepseek-chat] )
