2025-08-12 10:21:51 [nitro@ryzen5] git remote -v outputs multiple lines, can it list single endpoint?
2025-08-12 10:22:03 [deepseek-chat] Here's the cleanest single-line solution to show just one unique endpoint per remote (fetch
2025-08-12 10:22:03 [deepseek-chat] URL only):
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] for /f "tokens=2 delims= " %%U in ('git -C "%%D" remote -v ^| findstr "fetch" ^| head -1') do echo %%U
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] Breakdown:
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] 1. `findstr "fetch"` - Filters only fetch URLs
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] 2. `head -1` - Takes just the first result (Unix tool, use `more +1` on Windows if needed)
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] 3. `tokens=2` - Extracts just the URL (second token)
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] Pure Windows alternative (no external tools):
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] for /f "tokens=1,2 delims= " %%A in ('git -C "%%D" remote -v') do if "%%C"=="(fetch)" set "remote=%%B" & goto :done
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] :done
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] echo !remote!
2025-08-12 10:22:04 [deepseek-chat] Example Output:
