2025-08-12 11:18:59 [grok-4-0709] Yes, this machinespec update integrates three new providers (nuance, acapela, cereproc) directly
2025-08-12 11:18:59 [grok-4-0709] into "AI-voices"—a solid expansion! It's different from the initial version (adds ~3 providers) and
2025-08-12 11:18:59 [grok-4-0709] my suggested "additional-providers" block (which had 5, including google_cloud and coqui). If you'd
2025-08-12 11:18:59 [grok-4-0709] like to add the rest, refine, or tag it, let me know!
2025-08-12 11:19:21 [nitro@ryzen5] tell me about coqui
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] Coqui TTS is an open-source text-to-speech (TTS) system developed by Coqui AI (homepage:
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] https://coqui.ai), focused on high-quality, neural-based voice synthesis. It's built on projects
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] like Mozilla TTS and emphasizes accessibility, customization, and community-driven development.
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] Key Features:
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] - Voices: Uses datasets like LJSpeech (English-focused) or VCTK for multi-speaker models.
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] You can train custom voices with your own data.
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] - Languages: Strong in en-US, but extensible to others (e.g., fr-FR, ja-JP) via training.
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] Not as broad as commercial providers out-of-the-box.
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] - Synthesis: Neural models for natural-sounding speech; supports SSML for prosody control.
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] - Metadata: Styles like neural/customizable; ideal for open-source flexibility in research,
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] apps, or indie projects.
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] - Usage: Free for non-commercial use; great for developers—install via pip, train models,
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] or use pre-trained ones. It's popular in AI ethics circles for being transparent and
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] non-proprietary.
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] It's a gap-filler in machinespec for open-source options. If you'd like to add it fully to the
2025-08-12 11:19:32 [grok-4-0709] JSON, fetch more details, or tag it, just say!
2025-08-12 11:20:19 [nitro@ryzen5] ok lets add it
