2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] Thank you for sharing the updated subroutine. Yes, that looks correct for addressing the delayed
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] expansion issue—using `setlocal enabledelayedexpansion` and `!variable!` in the `echo` should
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] ensure the values are evaluated and attributed to the right repo.
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] However, a couple of notes for robustness:
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] - The `for` loop still captures values from every "File(s)" line in subdirectory summaries,
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] overwriting until the last one (not the grand total). To fix this, you could pipe to `findstr /E
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] "File(s)"` or parse only the final total line (e.g., check if `%%m` == "file(s)" and `%%n` ==
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] "bytes"` for the grand total).
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] - Consider changing `/-c` to `/-C` (uppercase) to reliably suppress commas in sizes, preventing CSV
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] breakage.
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] - `dir_count` is unused, so it could be removed.
2025-08-12 19:39:07 [grok-4-0709] If you'd like me to provide a fully revised script with these adjustments, just let me know!
