2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709] Yes, Markdown supports nested lists (unordered or ordered) by indenting inner items (use 2-4 spaces
2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709] or a tab). Example:
2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709] - Outer item 1
2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709]   - Inner item A
2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709]   - Inner item B
2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709] - Outer item 2
2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709]   1. Inner numbered 1
2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709]   2. Inner numbered 2
2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709] This works in most Markdown renderers (e.g., GitHub, CommonMark). If you need it for your spec
2025-08-13 08:58:54 [grok-4-0709] docs, let me know!
