2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709] Why These Suggestions?
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709] - Earliest Focus: All predate 1960, starting from the 1920s electronic dawn. They represent
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709] key milestones in audio circuit history (e.g., from tubes to transistors).
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709] - Connection to Pinball/Arcade:
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709]   - Emphasize evolution: Theremin's oscillators → Hammond's mechanical tones → Transistor amps →
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709] Gottlieb's RC chimes (1960) → Digital boards like Defender (1981).
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709]   - These laid the groundwork for game audio (e.g., timed effects, amplification).
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709] - Minimal Detail: Kept to core fields, with brief `notes` for context. No deep schematics
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709] or values—expand later if needed.
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709] - Relevance: Selected for influence on soldered circuitry (e.g., vacuum tubes in early
2025-08-13 10:06:45 [grok-4-0709] synths mirrored pinball's electromechanical simplicity).
