2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] claude-sonnet-4-20250514: Deno has limited clipboard support:
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] • Reading Clipboard*
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] - No native clipboard API in Deno runtime
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] - Can shell out to OS commands: `pbpaste` (macOS), `xclip` (Linux), `powershell Get-Clipboard`
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] (Windows)
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] • Writing to Clipboard*
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] - Same approach - shell to `pbcopy`, `xclip -selection clipboard`, `clip.exe`
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] - Web APIs like `navigator.clipboard` aren't available in Deno's runtime
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] • Terminal Integration*
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] - ANSI escape sequences can trigger some terminal clipboard operations
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] - OSC 52 sequence can write to clipboard in some terminals
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] - Raw mode input can detect paste operations but not read clipboard directly
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] For your copy button feature, you'd likely need:
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] async function copyToClipboard(text: string) {
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4]     const cmd = Deno.build.os === "windows"
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4]         ? ["powershell", "-c", `Set-Clipboard "${text}"`]
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4]         : Deno.build.os === "darwin"
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4]         ? ["pbcopy"]
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4]         : ["xclip", "-selection", "clipboard"];
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4]     const proc = new Deno.Command(cmd[0], {args: cmd.slice(1), stdin: "piped"});
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4]     // ...
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] }
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] The raw mode paste issues you mentioned are probably related to terminal escape sequence parsing
2025-08-13 10:43:22 [claude-sonnet-4] rather than actual clipboard access.
