2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] claude-sonnet-4-20250514: claude-sonnet-4-20250514: Not a dumb question at all - console tab
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] support is inconsistent:
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] • Traditional Consoles*
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] - Most support tab characters (`\t`) for display
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] - Tab width varies (usually 8 spaces, sometimes 4)
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] - No guarantee of consistent alignment across different terminals
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] • Your Code Context*
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] - You're already using spaces for indentation in `mdToAnsi()`
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] - The `quoteString()` function uses `"\t"+line`
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] - ANSI formatting can mess with tab positioning
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] • Better Approach*
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] - Convert tabs to spaces for predictable alignment
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] - Use fixed-width formatting for tables/code blocks
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] - Your current space-based indentation is more reliable
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] Given that your tool outputs formatted tables and code blocks, sticking with spaces gives you
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] better control over visual alignment. Tabs would be unpredictable across different terminal
2025-08-13 10:45:10 [claude-sonnet-4] configurations.
