2025-08-13 12:56:31 [nitro@ryzen5] can i add a signal handler or something, what are all my options for out of band user command like escape
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] In Deno, you have several options to handle out-of-band user commands (like `ESC` key) alongside
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] normal input:
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] 1. Signal Handlers (Limited)
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    - Only works for OS signals (not keystrokes):
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    Deno.addSignalListener("SIGINT", () => {
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      console.log("\nCtrl+C pressed - custom handler");
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      // Handle cleanup
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    });
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] 2. Raw Mode (Unstable)
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    - Your current approach with `Deno.stdin.setRaw(true)` is the only way to detect individual keys
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] like `ESC`.
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    - Example:
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    Deno.stdin.setRaw(true);
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    const buf = new Uint8Array(3);
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    while (true) {
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      const n = await Deno.stdin.read(buf);
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      if (n === null) break;
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      if (buf[0] === 27) { // ESC key
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]        console.log("ESC pressed!");
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      }
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    }
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] 3. Hybrid Approach
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    - Use `prompt()` for normal input but periodically check for signals/escape:
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    let escapePressed = false;
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    // Simulate escape check (would need raw mode)
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    const checkEscape = async () => {
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      const buf = new Uint8Array(1);
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      while (true) {
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]        const n = await Deno.stdin.read(buf);
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]        if (n === null) break;
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]        if (buf[0] === 27) escapePressed = true;
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      }
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    };
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    // Main input loop
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    while (true) {
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      const input = prompt("> ");
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      if (escapePressed) {
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]        console.log("Aborting via ESC!");
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]        break;
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      }
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]      // Process input...
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat]    }
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] Key Notes:
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] - No native `ESC` detection without raw mode.
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] - Signals only handle `SIGINT` (Ctrl+C) and a few others.
2025-08-13 12:56:53 [deepseek-chat] - For true out-of-band commands, raw mode is unavoidable.
