2025-08-13 13:12:38 [deepseek-chat] The string `const noSpace="​‌‍";` contains three invisible Unicode characters:
2025-08-13 13:12:38 [deepseek-chat] 1. `U+200B` - Zero Width Space
2025-08-13 13:12:38 [deepseek-chat] 2. `U+200C` - Zero Width Non-Joiner
2025-08-13 13:12:38 [deepseek-chat] 3. `U+200D` - Zero Width Joiner
2025-08-13 13:12:38 [deepseek-chat] These are all zero-width/control characters used for text formatting in various scripts.
2025-08-13 13:12:58 [nitro@ryzen5] can you explain the behavior of each
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat] Certainly! Here's a brief explanation of each zero-width character in your string:
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat] 1. `U+200B` (Zero Width Space)
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat]    - Invisible space that allows line breaks but doesn't affect word separation.
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat]    - Used for wrapping long words in HTML/CSS.
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat] 2. `U+200C` (Zero Width Non-Joiner, ZWNJ)
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat]    - Prevents ligatures/joining of adjacent characters (e.g., in Arabic or Indic scripts).
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat]    - Example: `فا` + ZWNJ + `ن` → "فا‌ن" (prevents cursive joining).
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat] 3. `U+200D` (Zero Width Joiner, ZWJ)
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat]    - Forces connected rendering (e.g., emoji sequences like 👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 or Arabic script).
2025-08-13 13:13:11 [deepseek-chat]    - Example: `👨` + ZWJ + `👩` → "👨‍👩" (combines into a single glyph).
2025-08-13 13:13:12 [deepseek-chat] All three are invisible but affect text layout/rendering. Let me know if you'd like code to detect
2025-08-13 13:13:12 [deepseek-chat] them!
