2025-08-13 15:03:42 [nitro@ryzen5] can new implentation live side by side?
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711] Yes.  Below is a minimal, zero-side-effect way to confirm the current single-thread code is
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711] bug-free before you graft the new concurrent layer.
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711] 1. Freeze a regress-test snapshot
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    cp forge.json forge.json.BACKUP
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    deno task --allow-all slopfountain.ts <<'END'
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    /reset yes           # factory reset to deterministic state
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    /list model
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    /help 0
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    say hello
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    END
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    Run this three times.  The final `forge.json` must be exactly the same each run (differs
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711] by ≤ 1 byte → bug).  This validates all the parts we care about:
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    - `sharedFiles` duplicate-detection
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    - counters don’t double-count or drift
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    - log lines are appended deterministically
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    - timestamp generation (epoch offset) is stable
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711] 2. Assert idempotence in code
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    Drop these two lines into `chat()` right after `await callCommand()` is processed:
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    const current = JSON.stringify(roha, null, "\t");
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    if (roha.counters.calls > 0 && current !== lastJSON) {
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]        console.error(`⚠️ Mutability @ call ${roha.counters.calls}`);
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    }
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    let lastJSON = current;
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    Re-run the test: any console-assert-failure = hidden mutable side-effect → fix first.
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711] 3. Concurrent replacement can coexist safely
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    Make the new dispatcher an optional second entry-point:
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    // slopfountain.ts minor patch
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    import { main } from "./slopfountain.ts";
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    import "./listener.ts";  // file with all the new session logic
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    deno run --allow-all --unstable slopfountain.ts           # still works
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    deno run --allow-all --unstable slopfountain.ts :8081     # new multi-session server
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711]    therefore you keep both modes and can bisect bugs easily.
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711] Once the deterministic back-flip test passes you know the single-user path is solid; the dispatcher
2025-08-13 15:04:11 [kimi-k2-0711] only adds asynchronous gravy on top.
