2025-08-14 13:35:31 [deepseek-chat] points:
2025-08-14 13:35:31 [deepseek-chat] 1. Shortcodes (like `:smile:`) are typically for inline emoji/icon insertion
2025-08-14 13:35:31 [deepseek-chat] 2. Markdown code blocks (```) are for multi-line code snippets
2025-08-14 13:35:32 [deepseek-chat] 3. They serve different purposes and have different syntax requirements
2025-08-14 13:35:32 [deepseek-chat] Best practice would be to:
2025-08-14 13:35:32 [deepseek-chat] - Keep them as separate features
2025-08-14 13:35:32 [deepseek-chat] - Document their distinct use cases
2025-08-14 13:35:32 [deepseek-chat] - Consider adding a syntax prefix (like `:` for shortcodes vs ``` for code blocks)
2025-08-14 13:35:32 [deepseek-chat] This maintains clarity while allowing both features to coexist. Would you like me to suggest
2025-08-14 13:35:32 [deepseek-chat] specific syntax rules for shortcodes?
2025-08-14 13:38:12 [nitro@ryzen5] line=replaceShortCodes(line);
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] Yes, adding a `replaceShortCodes()` function would be a clean way to handle shortcode processing
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] separately from markdown. Here's a simple implementation approach:
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] function replaceShortCodes(text: string): string {
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat]   // Match :shortcode: patterns
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat]   return text.replace(/:([a-z_]+):/g, (match, code) => {
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat]     return bibli.spec.shortcode[code] || match; // Fallback to original if not found
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat]   });
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] }
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] Key benefits:
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] 1. Processes `:smile:` independently of markdown
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] 2. Works inline within text
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] 3. Falls back gracefully if shortcode isn't defined
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] You'd call it before markdown processing:
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] line = replaceShortCodes(line);
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] line = mdToAnsi(line); // Then process markdown
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] This keeps the concerns separated while maintaining both features. Would you like me to suggest any
2025-08-14 13:38:28 [deepseek-chat] additional shortcode features?
