2025-08-17 09:51:52 [nitro@ryzen5] the cursor still treats heart shortcode once replaced as single width in the vscode terminal
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat] Ah, I see the issue! When you replace a shortcode like `:heart:` with ❤️ in the terminal, VSCode's
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat] terminal (and many terminals) still treats the emoji as single-width, even though some
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat] emoji visually appear wider. This is a common terminal rendering quirk.
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat] Why This Happens:
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat] 1. Terminal Emulators often use legacy "cell-based" rendering where each character occupies
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat] 1 or 2 fixed-width cells.
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat] 2. Emoji Width Ambiguity:
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat]    - Many emoji (like ❤️) are technically single-width in Unicode (`EAST ASIAN WIDTH=Neutral`).
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat]    - But some terminals render them wider for aesthetics (e.g., ❤️ vs. `A`).
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat] 3. VSCode Terminal uses a modified version of xterm.js, which follows classic terminal
2025-08-17 09:52:23 [deepseek-chat] width rules strictly.
