2025-08-18 12:56:06 [nitro@ryzen5] i want to backspace the cursor over a tab, so should i push a bunch of 0x08 ?
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] For backspacing over tabs, you'll want to:
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] 1. Calculate visual tab width based on cursor position
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] 2. Generate the correct number of backspace sequences (0x08)
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] Here's the improved tab backspace logic:
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] function backspace(bytes: number[]) {
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]   if (!grapheme.length) return;
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]   const lastChar = grapheme.pop()!;
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]   const isTab = (lastChar === "\t");
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]   if (isTab) {
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     // Calculate visual position before tab
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     const pos = stringWidth(grapheme.join(""));
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     // Determine how many spaces to backspace (1-8)
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     const spaces = TabWidth - (pos % TabWidth);
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     // Generate backspace sequences
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     for (let i = 0; i < spaces; i++) {
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]       bytes.push(0x08); // Just backspace, no space-overwrite
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     }
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]   } else {
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     // Normal character backspace
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     const width = stringWidth(lastChar) || 1;
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     for (let i = 0; i < width; i++) {
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]       bytes.push(0x08, 0x20, 0x08); // Backspace, space, backspace
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]     }
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat]   }
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] }
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] Key improvements:
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] - Properly handles mid-tab positions
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] - Only uses backspace (0x08) for tabs since they're single characters
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] - Maintains existing space-overwrite behavior for normal chars
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] - More accurate cursor positioning
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] Note: This assumes your terminal handles backspacing over tabs correctly. Some terminals may need
2025-08-18 12:56:24 [deepseek-chat] additional handling.
