2025-08-19 10:10:15 [deepseek-chat] Yes, in DOS/Windows command line:
2025-08-19 10:10:15 [deepseek-chat] - Use backslashes `\` for paths instead of forward slashes `/`
2025-08-19 10:10:15 [deepseek-chat] - Example: `C:\Users\Name\file.txt` instead of `C:/Users/Name/file.txt`
2025-08-19 10:10:15 [deepseek-chat] Key notes:
2025-08-19 10:10:15 [deepseek-chat] 1. Some modern Windows apps accept `/` but `\` is the native DOS format
2025-08-19 10:10:15 [deepseek-chat] 2. To avoid issues with escape characters, you can:
2025-08-19 10:10:15 [deepseek-chat]    - Use double backslashes `\\` in code
2025-08-19 10:10:15 [deepseek-chat]    - Or use raw strings like `r"C:\path"` in Python
