2025-08-19 13:33:57 [nitro@ryzen5] what is csi 50 50 in terms of response from ansi dsr?
2025-08-19 13:34:07 [deepseek-chat] In ANSI DSR (Device Status Report), CSI 50 50 refers to a "Printer OK" response.
2025-08-19 13:34:07 [deepseek-chat] Here’s a quick breakdown:
2025-08-19 13:34:07 [deepseek-chat] - CSI (Control Sequence Introducer): `ESC [`
2025-08-19 13:34:07 [deepseek-chat] - 50 50: Indicates the printer is ready (no errors).
2025-08-19 13:34:07 [deepseek-chat] If the printer were busy or had an error, different codes (like `51` or `53`) would be returned.
2025-08-19 13:34:07 [deepseek-chat] Let me know if you'd like deeper details!
