2025-08-20 08:20:56 [deepseek-chat] Yes, that's the correct approach. On macOS (and Unix systems in general), terminal input is often
2025-08-20 08:20:56 [deepseek-chat] buffered and can deliver multiple escape sequences in a single read operation. Since these
2025-08-20 08:20:56 [deepseek-chat] sequences may not be individually terminated or framed by packet boundaries, you should:
2025-08-20 08:20:56 [deepseek-chat] 1. Read available data into a buffer
2025-08-20 08:20:56 [deepseek-chat] 2. Scan for the next ESC character (ASCII 27, or `\x1b`) to delineate sequences
2025-08-20 08:20:56 [deepseek-chat] 3. Process each complete sequence between ESC characters
2025-08-20 08:20:56 [deepseek-chat] This allows you to handle multiple concatenated CSI sequences arriving in a single read call.
