2025-08-20 08:34:21 [deepseek-chat] The character with code 126 is the tilde: `~`
2025-08-20 08:34:21 [deepseek-chat] In ANSI and ASCII encoding:
2025-08-20 08:34:21 [deepseek-chat] - Decimal: 126
2025-08-20 08:34:21 [deepseek-chat] - Hexadecimal: 0x7E
2025-08-20 08:34:21 [deepseek-chat] - Character: ~
2025-08-20 08:34:21 [deepseek-chat] - Common name: Tilde
2025-08-20 08:34:21 [deepseek-chat] It's often used in terminals for home directory expansion (e.g., `~/Documents`) and in various
2025-08-20 08:34:21 [deepseek-chat] programming contexts.
2025-08-20 08:42:19 [nitro@ryzen5] distinct? or destinct?
2025-08-20 08:42:27 [deepseek-chat] The correct spelling is distinct.
2025-08-20 08:42:27 [deepseek-chat] • Distinct* means:
2025-08-20 08:42:27 [deepseek-chat] - Clearly different or separate
2025-08-20 08:42:27 [deepseek-chat] - Recognizably individual
2025-08-20 08:42:27 [deepseek-chat] - Well-defined
2025-08-20 08:42:27 [deepseek-chat] • Destinct* is not a valid English word - it's a common misspelling of "distinct."
2025-08-20 08:42:27 [deepseek-chat] Examples:
2025-08-20 08:42:27 [deepseek-chat] - "They have distinct personalities"
2025-08-20 08:42:27 [deepseek-chat] - "Each model has distinct capabilities"
