2025-08-20 09:04:56 [nitro@ryzen5] why is 22 missing, what is history of these codes, do they have periods in history?
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] Short answer: 22 is simply unused in the common VT/ANSI mapping — the numbers were chosen
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] historically and have gaps, not because of a mathematical pattern.
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] Why:
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] - VT100 originally provided only a few function keys (F1–F4) as ESC O P..S.
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] - When DEC/ANSI terminals expanded keys (VT220 and later), they introduced CSI (ESC [) numeric
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] forms like CSI 15 ~, CSI 17 ~, etc. Those numeric codes were chosen to avoid collisions with
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] existing sequences and to match the terminal vendor’s internal key tables, not to make a contiguous
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] sequence. That left gaps (e.g., 16 and 22) which were never assigned in the common mapping.
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] Different terminals filled or reused gaps differently, so there’s no single continuous standard
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] that includes 22.
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] - Terminfo/termcap and xterm adopted the VT mappings (F5..F12 → CSI
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] 15~,17~,18~,19~,20~,21~,23~,24~). That’s why you see 15,17,18,19,20,21,23,24 and no 16 or 22.
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] About “periods”:
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] - Escape sequences use characters like ESC, “[”, digits, “;” (parameter separator), letters or “~”
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] as terminators. They do not use “.” (period) as a syntactic separator in standard CSI/SS3
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] sequences. If you see dots in docs, they’re usually typographic/ellipses, not literal bytes.
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] If you want the normal F1–F12 mappings to include in JSON, use (prefixes implied):
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] - F1..F4: ESC O P / Q / R / S
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] - F5..F12: ESC [ 15~ / 17~ / 18~ / 19~ / 20~ / 21~ / 23~ / 24~
2025-08-20 09:05:32 [gpt-5-mini] Tell me if you want those returned as full escape strings or as suffixes you can concatenate.
