2025-08-20 09:12:04 [nitro@ryzen5] in plain dos is there keyboard shortcuts?
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] Yes — plain DOS (COMMAND.COM / MS‑DOS) has several built‑in keyboard shortcuts, mostly for
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] interrupting programs and for command‑line editing/history. Common ones:
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] Interrupts and flow control
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Ctrl+C or Ctrl+Break — interrupt/terminate the running program (if it supports it).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Ctrl+S — pause output (XOFF).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Ctrl+Q — resume output (XON).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Ctrl+Z — end‑of‑file marker (can be typed on a line to mark EOF in files).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Ctrl+Alt+Del — soft reboot (depends on hardware/VM).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] COMMAND.COM (command line) editing & history shortcuts
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - F1 — retype previous command one character at a time (press repeatedly to add more).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - F2 <char> — copy previous command up to (but not including) the next occurrence of <char>.
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - F3 — repeat the previous command (whole).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - F4 <char> — delete from current cursor position up to the next occurrence of <char>.
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - F5 — repeat the previous command (alias of F3 on many versions).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - F6 — insert Ctrl+Z (EOF) into the line.
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - F7 — display command history (numbered list).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - F8 — cycle backward through command history, matching what you’ve typed so far.
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - F9 — type the number of a history entry (from F7) to recall it.
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Alt+F7 — clear the command history (on many DOS versions).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] Other keys
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Ins — toggle insert mode (depends on environment).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Home / End / PgUp / PgDn / ← → — move cursor in environments that support line editing.
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Tab completion is not native to classic COMMAND.COM (present in later shells like cmd.exe).
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] Notes
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Exact behavior varies by MS‑DOS version, COMMAND.COM build, or DOS clone (FreeDOS), and by
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] running in a Windows console or DOSBox where host terminal may change keys.
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] - Tell me which DOS (MS‑DOS version, FreeDOS, DOSBox, or Windows cmd.exe) you’re using if you want
2025-08-20 09:12:22 [gpt-5-mini] precise behavior or how to test specific keys.
