2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] Yes, you can add a timeout to `reader.read()` using `Promise.race()` to debounce or prevent hangs
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] (e.g., during rapid pastes). This wraps the read in a race against a timeout promise, allowing you
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] to handle stalled inputs gracefully. Here's a concise implementation for your `rawPrompt`
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] loop—adjust the timeout (e.g., 100ms) as needed for debounce feel:
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] // Inside your rawPrompt while loop
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] try {
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]   const readPromise = reader.read();
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]   const timeoutPromise = new Promise((_, reject) =>
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]     setTimeout(() => reject(new Error("Read timeout")), 100) // Debounce timeout in ms
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]   );
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]   const { value, done } = await Promise.race([readPromise, timeoutPromise])
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]     .catch((err) => {
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]       if (err.message === "Read timeout") {
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]         // Handle debounce: e.g., ignore or flush buffer
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]         console.log("[RAW] Debounce timeout - ignoring rapid input");
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]         return { value: null, done: false }; // Continue loop without breaking
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]       }
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]       throw err; // Propagate other errors
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]     });
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]   if (done || !value) break;
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]   // Rest of your byte processing...
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] } catch (error) {
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]   console.error("Prompt error:", error);
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709]   busy = false;
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] }
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] This debounces by timing out rapid reads (useful for paste floods), preventing multiline blank line
2025-08-20 14:04:43 [grok-4-0709] issues. Test with pastes; if you need full integration or tweaks, provide more context!
