2025-08-21 19:53:49 [nitro@ryzen5] hi kimi can you help, am trying to fix appearance if emoji when slopshop calls writeMessage
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] Looking at the issue, the problem is that `writeMessage()` blindly writes raw text without
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] processing shortcodes, while the interactive `slopPrompt()` does this expansion during input.
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] `writeMessage()` should pass the text through the same short-code → emoji path.
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] Add a tiny utility:
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] // ---------- in sloprawprompt.ts ----------
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] export function expandShortCodes(text: string): string {
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711]   return text.replace(
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711]     /:([a-z0-9_]+):/g,
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711]     (_, tag) => shortcode[tag.toLowerCase()] ?? `:${tag}:`
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711]   );
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] }
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] // ----------------------------------------------------------
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] Then change `writeMessage()` to apply the expansion before it writes:
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] export async function writeMessage(message: string){
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711]   const expanded = expandShortCodes(message);
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711]   await writer.write(encoder.encode(expanded));
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711]   await writer.ready;
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] }
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] That one-line change makes any string produced by slopshop (after it has been handed to
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] `writeMessage` via `slopPrompt`) look identical to what the interactive side shows.
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] If you also want to keep the wrapper you added for combined ANSI-printing + emoji-expansion, you
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] could instead apply `expandShortCodes` right before you hand the text to `writeMessage`, e.g.:
2025-08-21 19:54:17 [kimi-k2-0711] writeMessage(expandShortCodes(message));
