2025-08-21 20:12:53 [nitro@ryzen5] pasting emoji works in deno prompt, but raw mode on windows I am getting ??
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711] Raw mode on Windows doesn’t display anything outside the basic single-byte (SBCS) code page;
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711] everything is passed through byte-by-byte. Emoji (> U+007F) therefore get shown with fallback
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711] illegal-char sequences (`?`) because your console font/code page doesn’t recognise the UTF-8 bytes.
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711] Fix:
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711] - Switch the console to UTF-8
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711]   chcp 65001
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711]   and pick a font that actually contains emoji (e.g. “Segoe UI Emoji”).
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711] - Or pipe/redirect your program’s output and read it with a terminal that fully supports Unicode
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711] (Windows Terminal, Warp, WezTerm, ConEmu, etc.).
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711] After the encoding and font are correct, emoji will appear in Deno raw-mode REPL just as they did
2025-08-21 20:13:18 [kimi-k2-0711] in the default cooked mode.
2025-08-21 20:14:13 [nitro@ryzen5] that is not it, emoji display find, is is the pasting operation that is bugged
2025-08-21 20:14:27 [nitro@ryzen5] find=fine
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] Possible fix:
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] Launch the shell/REPL with a true UTF-8 console and tell the Windows API you expect UTF-8
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] input (what Deno currently omits in raw mode).
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] Quick work-around you can use today:
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] :: launch a real UTF-8 terminal
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] chcp 65001 & set PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8   :: optional if python involved
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] wt                                        :: open Windows Terminal, cmd inside
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] Then:
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] deno --eval "console.log('😍')"
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] Pasting emoji (either via Ctrl-V or right-click) will now transmit the full UTF-8 sequence; Deno’s
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] raw-mode handler receives them instead of the “??” sequence you saw.
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] If you need to run `deno --repl --raw`, do it inside Windows Terminal as above for now; the bug
2025-08-21 20:14:43 [kimi-k2-0711] will be patched in a future Deno release.
