2025-08-22 08:16:58 [nitro@ryzen5] with fountain boxes a calendar would look good
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] Below is a “calendar card” you could drop anywhere in Fountain’s message stream.
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] Each box uses the same ANSI-line-drawing routine already in slopcity.ts / fountain (the
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] `boxChars[set]` arrays and helper helpers like `boxTop`, etc.).
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] It consumes a Date instance and prints a single‐month view that fits inside 78 columns and is
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] readable under both dark and bright terminals.
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] // === fountain-calendar.ts  (minimal harvest) ===
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] import {
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   padChars,
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   stringWidth,
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   boxChars,
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   CodeBlock as Code,
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   AnsiReset as ansiR
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] } from "./slopfountain.ts";
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] function padCenter(text, w) {
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const s = String(text);
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const fill = w - stringWidth(s);
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const l = Math.floor(fill / 2);
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   return " ".repeat(l) + s + " ".repeat(Math.max(w - l - s.length, 0));
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] }
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] function boxMonth(date = new Date()) {
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const year = date.getFullYear();
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const mon  = date.getMonth();
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const daysInMonth = new Date(year, mon + 1, 0).getDate();
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const first = new Date(year, mon, 1);
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const startWeekday = first.getDay();   // 0=Sun, 1=Mon…
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const box = boxChars[0];               // rounded boxes
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const ch = (s) => s;                   // future ansi helper placeholder
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   let rows = [];
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const title = `${date.toLocaleString("en-US", { month: "long", year: "numeric" })}`;
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const head = [ "Su", "Mo", "Tu", "We", "Th", "Fr", "Sa" ].map(c => padChars(c, " "));
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   // top
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   rows.push(ch(box.topLeft) + ch(box.horizontal).repeat(21) + ch(box.topRight));
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   // month label
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   rows.push(ch(box.vertical) + padCenter(title, 21) + ch(box.vertical));
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   rows.push(ch(box.verticalLeft) + ch(box.horizontal).repeat(21) + ch(box.verticalRight));
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   // weekday headers
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   const header = ch(box.vertical) + " " + head.join(" ") + " " + ch(box.vertical);
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   rows.push(header);
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   rows.push(ch(box.verticalLeft) + ch(box.horizontal).repeat(21) + ch(box.verticalRight));
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   // day cells
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   let day = 1;
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   for (let w = 0; w < 6; w++) {
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]     let cells = []
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]     for (let d = 0; d < 7; d++) {
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]       let text = "";
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]       if ((w === 0 && d < startWeekday) || day > daysInMonth) {
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]         text = padChars("  ", " ");
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]       } else {
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]         text = String(day).padStart(2, " ");
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]         day++;
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]       }
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]       cells.push(text);
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]     }
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]     const line = ch(box.vertical) + " " + cells.join(" ") + " " + ch(box.vertical);
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]     rows.push(line);
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   }
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   // bottom edge
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   rows.push(ch(box.bottomLeft) + ch(box.horizontal).repeat(21) + ch(box.bottomRight));
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711]   return rows.join("\n") + ansiR;
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] }
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] // usage
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] //
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] // echo(boxMonth());
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] Paste `boxMonth()` anywhere Fountain would `echo()` output (history dump, login banner, or injected
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] as a synthetic assistant message) and you’ll get a tidy boxed calendar that inherits the ANSI
2025-08-22 08:17:57 [kimi-k2-0711] kitchen already sprinkled across slop lands.
2025-08-22 08:18:58 [nitro@ryzen5] no code thanks, discussion only unless prompted
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] Got it—strictly discussion only.
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] A boxed monthly calendar would slot cleanly into Fountain’s “fancy status / welcome” tradition, but
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] `plan.txt` already flags a couple of high-level UX needs that dovetail with it:
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] - Mouse control. If the calendar were terminal-rendered by a worker, clicking on a day
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] could emit events Fountain can treat as commands—`/remind`, `/journal`, or tagging historical
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] dumps.
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] - copy button on code blocks / paste fixes. When you do box-drawing output like a calendar,
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] the stored string carries ANSI escape sequences; the Desktop clipboard breaks unless you strip
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] them. The same decoder used to fix «raw mode delete key» issues can double-duty for sane clipboard
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] copies.
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] The calendar is thematic, not critical: it satisfies the social interaction (“mindful of others”)
2025-08-22 08:19:14 [kimi-k2-0711] part if sessions start by showing a shared, neutral date stamp before any federated model talk.
