2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] What happened (summary)
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - Primary failure: InvalidData: "Windows stdio in console mode does not support writing non‑UTF‑8
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] byte sequences". That came from writer.write/TextEncoder writes while rawprompt was enabled.
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - Secondary failure: BadResource: a console/log attempt ran after a resource (stdout/writer/reader)
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] had been closed or dropped during error recovery (exitForge path).
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - In short: code wrote bytes the Windows console rejected, threw; cleanup then tried to use closed
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] I/O objects and crashed again.
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] Likely root causes
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - rawprompt writes binary-like sequences (mixed terminal control bytes, pasted data,
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] bracketed-paste markers, or arbitrary Uint8Array) directly to stdout. On Windows console mode those
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] writes can be rejected if the bytes are not valid UTF‑8 the environment expects.
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - Some writes are genuinely binary (audio, framed worker payloads) and should not go to stdout.
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - Error/exception handling closes or nulls writers/readers but other code still assumes they exist
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] (exitForge uses console/streams after they’ve been closed).
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] Short, practical fixes (pick any)
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - Immediate mitigation: disable rawprompt on Windows:
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini]   - if (Deno.build.os === "windows") roha.config.rawprompt = false;
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini]   - This will stop problematic low-level writes while you debug paste/emoji handling.
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - Sanitize all text writes to stdout:
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini]   - Always pass strings through TextEncoder.encode; catch InvalidData and fall back to console.log
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] or replace invalid chars (normalize + replace non-printables).
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - Avoid writing raw binary to stdout:
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini]   - Route audio/inline-data to files (save/send) instead of writer.write to console.
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - Guard writes and cleanup:
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini]   - Wrap writer.read/write and console operations in try/catch.
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini]   - Before using writer/reader, test they’re not closed/null. In exitForge, ensure cleanup runs in
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] a finally and avoid logging to closed streams.
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini] - Add logging to find the offending write:
2025-08-22 09:45:17 [gpt-5-mini]   - Temporarily wrap writer.write to log the string length, first ~64 bytes (hex) and source
