2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] characters split incorrectly or non‑UTF‑8 sequences, Windows console may throw InvalidData. For
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] text input, prefer encoding strings with TextEncoder so you get valid UTF‑8.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - Encoding vs raw bytes: are you deliberately sending control/ANSI sequences and binary bytes? If
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] yes, raw bytes are appropriate. If you intend textual output, pass encoded UTF‑8.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] Resources & lifecycle
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - Ensure writer is open (not closed) before writing. Writing to a closed writer raises BadResource
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] / other errors at runtime.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - Serialisation: avoid concurrent writes from multiple places. Awaiting writer.write is usually
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] sufficient to serialize; awaiting both write and writer.ready is redundant and may complicate flow.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] Backpressure & performance
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - writer.write returns a Promise that resolves when the chunk is accepted. writer.ready is the
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] underlying ready promise for the stream; awaiting the write is normally enough.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - Converting bytes to a new Uint8Array each time allocates memory. For very frequent/large writes
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] you may want to reuse buffers or batch writes.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] Error handling
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - Wrap writes in try/catch to handle InvalidData, NotAllowed, BadResource, etc. On Windows, catch
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] InvalidData and fall back to safe UTF‑8/text output or disable raw/binary writes.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - If a write fails, avoid assuming the writer is still usable — check/close appropriately.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] Atomicity & partial writes
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - The stream abstraction normally handles partial writes for you; a single writer.write of a
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] Uint8Array will be enqueued as one chunk. If you build the bytes array incrementally you must
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] ensure you build complete logical chunks (don’t split multibyte UTF‑8 characters across writes).
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] Recommendations
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - If output is text: convert using new TextEncoder().encode(string) to guarantee UTF‑8.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - If output is control sequences/ANSI: ensure sequences are valid UTF‑8 bytes; on Windows test for
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] InvalidData and fallback to safe output.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - Surround writer.write with try/catch; check writer.closed before writing.
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] - Serialize writes (single writer instance, await the write promise) rather than parallel writes;
2025-08-22 09:57:07 [gpt-5-mini] awaiting writer.write is sufficient—awaiting writer.ready too is typically unnecessary.
