2025-08-22 12:15:12 [deepseek-chat] (encoded as UTF-16) to the application, not the ASCII byte 63 ('?'). However, if the application or
2025-08-22 12:15:12 [deepseek-chat] context does not support Unicode, it might misinterpret or convert the characters, sometimes
2025-08-22 12:15:12 [deepseek-chat] resulting in a '?' (byte 63) being displayed or transmitted instead. This usually indicates an
2025-08-22 12:15:12 [deepseek-chat] encoding mismatch or lack of Unicode support.
